# Coding conventions

Source of the decisions: `docs/decisions/0000-language-and-build.md` (D0.3, D0.7, D0.8).

## Naming

| Element | Style | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Types, classes, structs, enums, type aliases | PascalCase | `TimingArc`, `PinDirection` |
| Functions and methods | PascalCase | `FindPin()`, `ArrivalTime()` |
| Variables and parameters | snake_case | `max_delay`, `load_pin` |
| Data members | snake_case + trailing `_` | `arcs_`, `time_unit_` |
| Constants and `enum class` values | `k` + PascalCase | `kMaxFanout`, `PinDirection::kInput` |
| Namespaces | lowercase snake_case | `sta`, `sta::liberty` |
| Macros (avoid) | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE with `STA_` prefix | `STA_ASSERT` |

## Files

- One main class per `.hpp` / `.cpp` pair, named after it in PascalCase: `TimingGraph.hpp`, `TimingGraph.cpp`.
- Tests: `<Class>Test.cpp` under `tests/`, mirroring the `src/` layout.
- Headers start with `#pragma once`.
- Include order, one blank line between groups: the file's own header, C++ standard library,
  third-party (`<tcl.h>`, `<gtest/gtest.h>`), project headers (`"liberty/LibertyReader.hpp"`, relative to `src/`).

## Formatting

- 2-space indentation, 80-column lines, opening braces on the same line.
- `.clang-format` is the authority once it exists; do not hand-format against it.

## C++ usage

- C++20, no compiler extensions, no C++20 modules.
- Ownership is explicit: `std::unique_ptr` for owners, references or raw pointers for non-owning access;
  no naked `new` / `delete`.
- Prefer `enum class`, `std::string_view` and `std::span` parameters, `const` correctness, `[[nodiscard]]`
  on functions whose result must be checked.
- Never `using namespace` in a header.

## Errors and messages (D0.8)

- Report errors by throwing the project exception types; never let an exception cross the Tcl C API.
- Every user-visible message goes through the message handler with an ID such as `LIB-012`.

## CMake

- Target-based: `target_include_directories`, `target_link_libraries`, `target_compile_options`;
  no global `include_directories` or `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS` edits.
- Lowercase command names.
